<title>USA: Vivus stock jumps on strong earnings.</title>
<headline>Vivus stock jumps on strong earnings.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK</dateline>
<text>
<p>The stock of Vivus Inc. jumped Wednesday after the maker of a treatment for male impotence reported earnings that more than doubled Wall Street estimates.</p>
<p>Vivus was up $5.125 at $46.50 in early morning trading on the Nasdaq.</p>
<p>The Menlo Park, Calif.-based company said it earned $9.6 million or 54 cents a share in the first quarter compared with a net loss of $6.2 million or 45 cents a share a year earlier.</p>
